---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { site, catalogueProducts } from "../../data.mjs";
import { polyMailerThicknessOptions } from "../../product-data.mjs";
import { approximateInches } from "../../mailer-options.mjs";
import { getProductVisual } from "../../product-images.mjs";
import packingSource from "../../assets/new-products/poly-mailers-apparel-packing.jpg";
const packing = await getProductVisual(packingSource);
const path = "/guides/mailer-size-for-clothing/";
const title = "How to Choose the Right Mailer Size for Clothing";
const modelChecks = {
  P03: "Nearly no nominal width or length allowance before 4 cm thickness and seams; do not assume it fits.",
  P04: "A candidate to check for usable inner space, flap closure and actual packed fit.",
  P05: "A larger candidate if P04 leaves too little working room; check whether extra space suits your packing process."
};
const exampleModels = catalogueProducts.find(product => product.slug === "poly-mailers").sizes.filter(([model]) => model in modelChecks);
const schema = { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "Article", headline: title, author: { "@id": `${site.origin}/#organization` }, publisher: { "@id": `${site.origin}/#organization` }, mainEntityOfPage: `${site.origin}${path}`, image: new URL(packing.imageFull, site.origin).toString(), datePublished: "2026-10-20", dateModified: "2026-11-11", inLanguage: "en" };
const breadcrumbs = { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", itemListElement: [{ "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: site.origin }, { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Buying Guides", item: `${site.origin}/guides/` }, { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Clothing mailer size", item: `${site.origin}${path}` }] };
---
<Layout title={`${title} | Welltroy`} description="Choose a poly mailer for a sweatshirt or clothing order. Measure the complete pack, compare P03-P05 outer sizes in cm and inches, and request fit-check samples." quoteProduct="poly-mailers" contactContext="Clothing mailer fit check" canonicalPath={path} schemas={[schema, breadcrumbs]} ogImage={packing.imageFull} ogImageAlt="Folded clothing being packed into a printed pink poly mailer">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/guides/">Buying Guides</a> / Clothing mailer size</div><p class="eyebrow">Clothing packaging guide</p><h1>{title}</h1><p class="lead">Fold and pack the garment as it will ship, then measure packed width, length and thickness. Compare those measurements with candidate mailers, allowing space for insertion and closure. Confirm usable inner dimensions and test a sample before ordering: the catalogue lists outer dimensions.</p><p class="muted">By Welltroy · Updated <time datetime="2026-11-11">11 November 2026</time></p><nav class="anchor-links" aria-label="In this guide"><a href="#sweatshirt">Sweatshirt sizing</a><a href="#measure">Measure</a><a href="#packing-reference">Packing reference</a><a href="#measurement-record">Record measurements</a><a href="#models">Compare models</a><a href="#film-thickness">Thickness units</a><a href="#film-thickness-check">Check film thickness</a><a href="#test">Test the fit</a><a href="#quote">Send a brief</a></nav></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container article-layout"><article class="article-main">
    <h2 id="sweatshirt">What Size Poly Mailer Do I Need for a Sweatshirt?</h2>
    <p><strong>Choose from the sweatshirt's packed width, length and thickness, including the hood, inner bag and inserts.</strong> There is no single mailer size for every sweatshirt or hoodie: the garment's size, fabric, fold and number of items change the fit. A clothing size label such as S, M or L does not establish the shipping-pack dimensions.</p>
    <p>Measure the full pack, compare candidate outer sizes in the table below, then request the usable inner dimensions and a sample. The 24 × 30 × 4 cm example is a separate hypothetical pack, not a standard sweatshirt size. Do not treat P04 or P05 as a fit guarantee for an unmeasured hoodie.</p>
    <p><strong>For T-shirts, mixed orders or several garments:</strong> repeat the same process with the complete parcel. Group orders by their measured packing needs; test the largest and thickest pack in each group before approving one bag size for that group.</p>
    <h2 id="measure">Measure the Actual Shipping Pack</h2>
    <ol><li>Fold the garment the way your team will pack it. Include any tissue, cardboard insert or <a href="/products/zipper-bags/">inner zipper bag</a> you plan to use.</li><li>Measure the widest width, longest length and greatest thickness of the finished pack. If one mailer will hold several garments, measure the full group.</li><li>Record how the item enters the bag, how much room the adhesive flap needs, and whether it can shift without stressing seams.</li><li>For multiple garment styles, measure the largest packed example for each shipping group rather than assuming one size covers all.</li></ol>
    <div class="guide-callout"><strong>Do not size from a flat garment alone.</strong> Thickness consumes usable space when the mailer wraps around the contents. Seams, lining and flap position reduce the practical opening or closing area. Ask for usable internal measurements for the exact proposed construction.</div>
    <div class="alert"><strong>Want a starting shortlist?</strong> Use the <a href="/products/poly-mailers/#size-comparison">packed-item size comparison tool</a> to compare width, length, thickness and an adjustable allowance with catalogue outer sizes. It excludes the flap from body length and lets you add a candidate plus the comparison assumptions to a quote brief. Confirm usable inner dimensions and sample fit before ordering.</div>
    <h2 id="measurement-record">What Measurements Should I Send for a Clothing Mailer?</h2>
    <p>Record the finished shipping pack for each garment group, with units, item count and inner packaging. Measure your actual T-shirt or hoodie after folding; the record below does not assign a standard bag size to a garment type.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Clothing mailer measurement record"><table><caption>Record one set for each pack you want to test</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Record</th><th scope="col">Include in your enquiry</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Garment group</th><td>T-shirt, hoodie or mixed order; garment size range and number of items in the parcel.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Complete pack</th><td>Width × length × greatest thickness, in cm or inches, including inner bags, tissue and inserts.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Bag candidate</th><td>Model if known; ask us to confirm usable inner dimensions, opening and flap closure.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Order version</th><td>Quantity for this size, bag color and artwork version, plus destination and target arrival date.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Sample result</th><td>Record insertion, closure, seam strain and excess movement; approve the complete packed sample before production.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
    <p><a class="text-link" href="/downloads/clothing-mailer-fit-record.txt" download>Download the editable clothing fit record (.txt) ↓</a></p><p><a class="button button-secondary" href="/quote/?product=poly-mailers#quote-form" data-quote-placement="content">Ask us to check my clothing pack</a></p>
    <h2 id="packing-reference">A Welltroy Apparel Packing Reference</h2>
    <figure class="packing-reference"><a href={packing.imageFull} target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="View the apparel packing photograph"><img src={packing.image} srcset={packing.imageSrcSet} sizes="(max-width: 760px) calc(100vw - 40px), 760px" width={packing.imageWidth} height={packing.imageHeight} alt="Folded clothing with inner wrapping being inserted into a pink strawberry-pattern poly mailer" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></a><figcaption>Apparel packing photograph supplied by Welltroy. Measure the garment together with the inner wrapping, inserts and other items you will ship.</figcaption></figure>
    <p>The photograph is a packing reference. No model or measured dimensions are assigned to this pictured pack; the numerical example below is illustrative and describes a separate hypothetical item.</p>
    <div class="guide-callout"><strong>See the complete apparel project.</strong><p>This packing photograph and the production photograph document the same completed Welltroy customer project, shared anonymously. <a href="/products/poly-mailers/#poly-mailer-case">View the strawberry-print apparel project →</a> for the production context and what to prepare for your own printed mailer.</p></div>
    <h2 id="models">Catalogue Example: 24 × 30 × 4 cm Packed Garment</h2>
    <p>This is an illustrative packed item, not a verified Welltroy order. The 2025 catalogue lists the following <a href="/products/poly-mailers/">Poly Mailers</a> dimensions as outer width × length + flap:</p>
    <p>The example pack is approximately <strong>9.45 × 11.81 × 1.57 inches</strong> (width × length × thickness). The bag's flap below is separate from its body length.</p>
    <p class="table-scroll-hint">Swipe or scroll the table to compare cm, inches and sample enquiry links.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Poly mailer catalogue size comparison for clothing"><table><caption class="sr-only">Catalogue outer sizes for three candidates, not verified garment fits</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Model / enquiry</th><th scope="col">Catalogue outer size (cm)</th><th scope="col">Approx. outer size (inches)</th><th scope="col">What the example suggests</th></tr></thead><tbody>{exampleModels.map(([model, size]) => <tr><th scope="row"><a class="text-link" data-quote-placement="content" href={'/quote/?product=poly-mailers&size='+encodeURIComponent(model+' — '+size)+'#quote-form'}>Ask about {model} →</a></th><td>{size}</td><td>{approximateInches(size)}</td><td>{modelChecks[model]}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
    <p>The “+ 5 cm” is the listed flap, not extra usable body length. These outer figures alone cannot establish fit, and no model above is a guaranteed recommendation. Ask us to confirm inner dimensions, tolerance, closure position, material and availability for the size you intend to order.</p>
    <h2 id="film-thickness">Film Thickness and Packed Thickness Are Different</h2>
    <p><strong>Packed thickness</strong> is the depth of your folded clothing together with its inner packaging. Include it when assessing the room needed inside a mailer. <strong>Film thickness</strong> describes one wall of the bag and is a separate material specification.</p>
    <p>Welltroy's poly mailer reference options are {polyMailerThicknessOptions.map(option => option.microns).join(", ")} μm per side. For example, 60 μm per side is 0.06 mm per side, approximately 2.36 mil per side. It does not describe the depth of a garment pack. Compare the <a href="/products/poly-mailers/#poly-mailer-thickness">single-wall film thickness table</a> and confirm the material, chosen option and tolerance in your quotation.</p>
    <h2 id="film-thickness-check">How Should I Check Single-Wall Bag Thickness?</h2>
    <p><strong>Agree what will be measured, how it will be measured and the acceptance limits before comparing readings.</strong> For a plain poly mailer or garment bag, one wall means one bag panel. Measuring the front and back together includes two walls; a fold, seam overlap or zipper adds a different construction. One wall can itself contain several bonded material layers.</p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Identify the sample and thickness basis.</strong> Record the product, bag version, material, finish and sample or batch reference. Mark which panel and area the film specification covers. Keep seams, folds, closures and any printed or textured areas identified separately in the agreed location plan.</li>
      <li><strong>Agree the method before checking.</strong> Ask the supplier or inspector to specify a suitable instrument, its calibration status, units, sample preparation and measurement conditions. For a contact method, agree the contact conditions and how compression of the film is controlled. Also agree which bags and locations will be checked, how many readings to take and the acceptance criteria.</li>
      <li><strong>Record the individual readings.</strong> Follow that method and location plan. Identify each bag and measurement point, and keep every reading with its unit. If an average or range is requested, retain the underlying readings so the result can be reviewed.</li>
      <li><strong>Compare with the written specification.</strong> Use the agreed limits and decision rule for that bag version. If a method, unit or measurement basis differs, flag it for review before deciding acceptance. Retain the record, photo references and approved sample together.</li>
    </ol>
    <div class="guide-callout"><strong>Keep bubble construction separate.</strong> A bubble mailer's exterior film, liner and overall thickness including bubbles describe different measurements. This single-wall film check does not establish the overall thickness or cushioning performance of a bubble mailer. Confirm the construction and method for the selected <a href="/guides/kraft-vs-poly-bubble-mailers/#film-and-liner">bubble mailer layers</a>.</div>
    <h3 id="film-thickness-record">What Should the Thickness Record Include?</h3>
    <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Single-wall film thickness inspection record"><table><caption>Agree the fields before inspecting a sample or delivery</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Record</th><th scope="col">Details to keep</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Bag and requirement</th><td>Product, version, sample or batch, material, surface, one-wall basis, target thickness, unit and specification revision.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Method and locations</th><td>Instrument and calibration reference, agreed preparation and contact conditions, bag selection, location plan and reading count.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Actual readings</th><td>Bag ID, point ID, reading and unit for every measurement; any agreed calculation and observations.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Review and decision</th><td>Agreed limits and decision rule, photo references, inspector and date, result, and any open question requiring review.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
    <p><a class="text-link" href="/downloads/single-wall-film-thickness-record.txt" download>Download the blank film thickness record (TXT) ↓</a></p>
    <p>This is a planning and recording checklist. The blank record supplies no default tolerance, sampling plan or test result. Confirm the method and acceptance criteria with the supplier or inspection team for your order.</p>
    <p class="muted">Method references: <a href="https://store.astm.org/d6988-26.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ASTM D6988</a> discusses film thickness measurement and does not set commercial quality-control sampling. <a href="https://store.astm.org/f2251-13r23.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ASTM F2251</a> covers contact measurements for flexible packaging and states that acceptance criteria should be agreed by the user and producer. These references do not establish a Welltroy order's test method or compliance.</p>
    <p>Use this record alongside your <a href="/guides/custom-mailer-sample-approval/#record">sample approval</a> and <a href="/guides/bulk-packaging-arrival-inspection/#inspect-bags">arrival inspection</a>. For a new quote, include the material, single-wall thickness basis, units and any required inspection method in the <a href="/quote/?product=poly-mailers#quote-form" data-quote-placement="content">poly mailer enquiry</a> or <a href="/quote/?product=zipper-bags#quote-form" data-quote-placement="content">garment bag enquiry</a>; leave unknown requirements for review.</p>
    <h2 id="test">Can I Use One Mailer Size for All Clothing Orders?</h2>
    <p><strong>Only after checking the different complete packs you intend to ship.</strong> A bag that closes around one T-shirt may be too tight for a thick hoodie or leave excess space around a smaller item. Compare insertion, closure and movement for each packing group, then record which approved bag is used for which order.</p>
    <ul><li>Insert the actual packed garment into a physical sample without forcing it.</li><li>Close the flap in the normal position; check that the adhesive lands securely and contents do not strain the seams.</li><li>Check presentation and movement inside the bag, then test normal fulfillment and shipping handling.</li><li>For rigid or delicate accessories, compare a <a href="/products/poly-bubble-mailers/">Poly Bubble Mailer</a> or additional protective packaging; test the complete pack.</li></ul>
    <p>For the difference between a plain and cushioned mailer, see <a href="/guides/choose-a-mailer/">Poly Mailers vs Bubble Mailers</a>.</p>
    <p>Keep a <a href="/guides/custom-mailer-sample-approval/#record">sample approval record</a> with the bag model, actual packed dimensions, insertion and closure observations, artwork version and retained sample. If the item mix or packing method changes, repeat the affected fit checks before approving one size for all orders.</p>
    <h2 id="quote">Send Measurements That Can Be Quoted</h2>
    <p>Tell us the garment type, packed width × length × thickness, items per parcel, candidate model if any, quantity per size and design, desired film and closure, print artwork, destination and target timing. If you do not know the mailer size, send packed item measurements and ask us to compare samples.</p><p>Download the <a href="/downloads/poly-mailer-logo-quote-brief.txt" download>editable poly mailer quote brief (.txt)</a> to record these details, then paste the completed brief into your enquiry or attach it with the artwork. Leave the model undecided if you need a sample recommendation.</p><p>After receiving proposals, use the <a href="/guides/compare-custom-mailer-quotes/">quote comparison worksheet</a> to check that each offer uses the same dimensions, single-wall film thickness and delivery scope.</p><a class="button" href="/quote/?product=poly-mailers#quote-form" data-quote-placement="content">Request a clothing mailer quote</a>
  </article><aside class="side-card"><p class="eyebrow">From the catalogue</p><h2>Related Packaging</h2><div class="guide-options"><a href="/products/poly-mailers/"><strong>Poly Mailers</strong><span>Compare listed models and ask for usable inner space</span></a><a href="/products/zipper-bags/"><strong>Zipper Bags</strong><span>Plan inner packaging before measuring the finished pack</span></a><a href="/products/poly-bubble-mailers/"><strong>Poly Bubble Mailers</strong><span>Consider cushioning for compact, sensitive contents</span></a></div><a class="text-link" href="/guides/custom-packaging-500-pieces/">See the custom quote checklist →</a></aside></div></section>
</Layout>
<style>.article-main{min-width:0}.article-main td{min-width:145px;vertical-align:top}.article-main th[scope="row"]{vertical-align:top}.article-main table{min-width:650px}.article-main li{margin:0 0 10px}.packing-reference{margin:28px 0;min-width:0}.packing-reference img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:12px}.packing-reference figcaption{font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;margin-top:10px}h2[id]{scroll-margin-top:120px}</style>
